{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>All this.</b> 'There is' means what is found occasionally, rarely. The sense of 'perishes in his righteousness' is that his righteousness causes him to perish, like one who fasts continually. And 'prolongs his days in his wickedness' means he prolongs days through his wickedness, that he eats and drinks and rejoices and makes pleasures for the body."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:06.530102264Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}